title: "Causal Ordering and Reconstructable Event Histories in Distributed Systems"
message: "Please cite the exact repository version or later Zenodo record that binds these files."
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Lohmann
    given-names: Ingolf
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher; QIK-VRT"
version: "1.0.0-candidate"
date-released: 2026-08-20
repository-code: "https://github.com/Goldkelch/qik-vrt"
abstract: >-
  A source-bound synthesis of causal ordering, logical and process-local time,
  provenance-aware event reconstruction, serialization, and effect acknowledgement
  in distributed systems, with a 47-language dissemination set. Established
  distributed-systems claims are separated from QIK-VRT primary-source research
  interpretation and from Wikipedia, Zenodo, arXiv, and IETF platform events.
keywords:
  - distributed systems
  - causal ordering
  - logical clocks
  - provenance
  - event reconstruction
  - effect acknowledgement
  - QIK-VRT
